:: Crater Expedition {"position":"2650,900","size":"100,100"}
The science team has been measuring radiation in the crater. Mars has a thin atmosphere, so much more radiation reaches the ground than on Earth. The detectors hold the data scientists need to keep astronauts safe, but their batteries are almost empty.

Your radiation suit is back at the base. Going to get it takes time, and the detectors keep running down.

How do you do the expedition?
[[Go back for the suit and stay longer->Crater Suit]]

[[Stay without the radiation shield.->Crater NoSuit]]




:: Crater Leave {"position":"2825,1075","size":"100,100"}



:: Crater NoSuit {"position":"2700,1075","size":"100,100"}
(set: $expedition_done to true)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

You stay out without the shield until every detector has finished.

(if: $roll <= 50)[
(set: $health to 0)

The radiation is far stronger than your body can take. Your legs give out, and the team carries you back to the base. The doctors do everything they can, but it's too late. You don't survive.

[[Continue->Game Over]]
]
(else:)[
(set: $data to it + 5)
(set: $health to it - 4)
(set: $energy to it - 1)

You bring back all the data, but the radiation leaves you weak and dizzy. You were lucky this time.

[[Back to the crater->Investigation Tent]]
]



:: Crater Suit {"position":"2575,1075","size":"100,100"}
(set: $expedition_done to true)
(set: $data to it + 5)
(set: $health to it - 1)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $equipment to it - 1)
(set: $time to it - 1)

You work for hours with your suit on. The detectors collect a good amount of data. The suit blocks part of the radiation, but not all of it, and your health drops a little.

[[Back to the crater->Investigation Tent]]


:: Disconnect All {"position":"1375,1100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $storm_done to true)

(set: $food to it - 2)
(set: $energy to it + 2)
(set: $food_lost to true)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

You turned everything off. The base stayed dark and cold all night, and the food in the freezer spoiled.

(if: $roll <= 30)[
(set: $equipment to it - 1)
(set: $equipment_damaged to true)

A small surge still reached the base, and one machine stopped working.
]
(else:)[
The equipment came through the storm fine.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Disconnect Science {"position":"1650,1100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $storm_done to true)

(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $data_lost to true)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

You shut down the science instruments and kept the essentials on. Tonight's data is lost.

(if: $roll <= 30)[
(set: $equipment to it - 1)
(set: $equipment_damaged to true)

A small surge still got through, and one machine stopped working.
]
(else:)[
Nothing else was damaged.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Expedition {"position":"2600,700","size":"100,100"}
<div class="scene">
<div class="scene-image scene-image-crater"></div>
<div class="scene-text">
INVESTIGATION CRATER

A huge round hole in the ground with steep rocky walls. Scientists come here to study how space affects the human body, and to find ways to treat and prevent the problems. The goal is to make space travel safer.

Missions to the Moon and Mars are longer, and that brings more risks:

1. More time floating in weightlessness.
2. More exposure to radiation.
3. Longer delays when talking to Earth.
4. Less help from Earth with food, supplies, and emergency medical care.
</div>
<div class="scene-buttons">
(if: $expedition_done is true)[
The expedition is over.

]
(else:)[
[[Start the expedition->Crater Expedition]]
]
[[Back to map->Mars Map]]
</div>
</div>


:: Game Over {"position":"2775,1300","size":"100,100"}

MISSION OVER

You didn't survive the radiation.

Out on Mars there is very little to block radiation from space. In a big dose, it damages the body's cells, and the body can't repair them fast enough. That's why astronauts wear protection, plan every trip outside, and follow strict limits on how much radiation they can take.

Look back at your choices. You chose the data over your safety, and the crew lost you.

What would you protect first next time?

[[Try the mission again->START]]


:: Garage Coordination {"position":"2325,1025","size":"100,100"}
(set: $garage_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

The path is planned and the software is up to date.

(if: $roll <= 40)[
(set: $comms_dip to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)

When the arm starts moving, it pulls a lot of power. The radio and the lights go out for a while, because nobody planned for it.
]
(else:)[
The power held up this time. Nobody checked how the arm would affect the other systems.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Garage Full {"position":"2075,1025","size":"100,100"}
(set: $garage_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $equipment to it +1)



You spend the day on every step. The systems are lined up, the cameras are placed, and the software is up to date. The arm moves the part without a problem.

The base is low on energy tonight.

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Garage Software {"position":"2200,1025","size":"100,100"}
(set: $garage_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

The systems are lined up and the arm's path is planned.

(if: $roll <= 40)[
(set: $robot_glitch to true)
(set: $equipment to it - 1)

Halfway through the job, the robot's software freezes. The arm stops in the middle of the move, and you have to restart it before it can finish.
]
(else:)[
The old software held up this time. It's still overdue for an update.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Greenhouse {"position":"1025,625","size":"100,100"}
GREENHOUSE

A long room with plants growing under bright purple lights. There's lettuce, potatoes, and radishes in trays, with pipes that carry water to each row.

This is where the crew gets part of its fresh food.

[[Check the plants->Greenhouse Mission]]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Greenhouse Cold {"position":"1150,900","size":"100,100"}
(set: $greenhouse_done to true)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

The humidity and lights are set to shutt down overnight to save energy and the room gets colder overnight.

(if: $roll <= 50)[
(set: $plants_stunted to true)
(set: $food to it - 2)

The cold slows the plants down. They stop growing, and the harvest will be much smaller.
]
(else:)[
The plants made it through the cold. They look a little pale, but they're alive.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Greenhouse Humid {"position":"1025,900","size":"100,100"}
(set: $greenhouse_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

The temperature and lights are set but the austronaut messed the humidity and the air stays too damp.

(if: $roll <= 50)[
(set: $mold_found to true)
(set: $food to it - 2)

By evening there's mold on one of the trays. You have to throw out the whole tray.
]
(else:)[
The plants handled the extra moisture. Nothing grew on them this time, but the risk is still there.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Greenhouse Mission {"position":"1025,750","size":"100,100"}
(if: $greenhouse_done is true)[
The greenhouse is stable for now.

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]
]
(else:)[
The panel shows three readings drifting: temperature, humidity, and lighting.

(if: $lab_result is "leaf")[The lab results said the plants are already stressed, so they're more sensitive today.]

You can set all three right, but it would use most of the energy you have left, If the conditions are not optimal it could harm the harvest.

[[Control all three. It uses a lot of energy.->Greenhouse perfect]]

[[Fix the temperature and the lighting. ->Greenhouse Humid]]

[[Fix the humidity and the lighting. ->Greenhouse Cold]]
]


:: Greenhouse perfect {"position":"900,900","size":"100,100"}
(set: $greenhouse_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 2)
(set: $food to it +1)

All the settings are perfect but it uses too much energy. The plants keep growing and the harvest is great.

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Habitat {"position":"400,825","size":"100,100"}
HABITAT

This is where the crew lives and sleeps. It's a sealed building with bunks, a small kitchen, and a control panel for air and power.

Along the back wall are the systems that keep everyone alive: the heating and air equipment, the computers, and the radio and navigation gear. They all need regular maintenance.

[[Check the maintenance panel->Habitat Mission]]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Habitat Full {"position":"225,1100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $habitat_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $time to it - 1)

You spend the afternoon checking every system, changing filters, and updating the computers. Everything passes.

Maintenance like this takes up a big part of an astronaut's time and energy on the space station.

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Habitat Mission {"position":"400,950","size":"100,100"}
(if: $habitat_done is true)[
The maintenance is done for today.

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]
]
(else:)[
The panel shows three systems due for service: temperature and life support, the computer network, and communication and navigation.

Servicing everything uses a lot of energy. A system that isn't serviced might fail, and a failure in any of them could put the whole base at risk.

[[Service everything. ->Habitat Full]]

[[Service only the life support. ->Habitat Partial]]

[[Skip the maintenance. ->Habitat Skip]]
]



:: Habitat Partial {"position":"375,1100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $habitat_done to true)
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

You service the heating and air systems. They're ready to run.

(if: $roll <= 25)[
(set: $network_failed to true)
(set: $equipment to it - 1)

That night the computer network crashes. The control panel goes blank, and the crew has to run the base by hand until it's rebooted.
]
(else-if: $roll <= 50)[
(set: $comms_failed to true)
(set: $equipment to it - 1)

Communication and navigation go down. The base can't reach Earth, and the rover can't find its way back until it's fixed.
]
(else:)[
Nothing else breaks this time. The other systems are still overdue for service.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Habitat Skip {"position":"525,1100","size":"100,100"}
(set: $habitat_done to true)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

You leave the maintenance for later.

(if: $roll <= 20)[
(set: $thermo_failed to true)
(set: $crew to it - 2)
(set: $energy to it - 1)

The heating and air system stops. The temperature drops and the air gets stale. The crew works through the night to restart it. A failure like this could cost the whole base.
]
(else-if: $roll <= 40)[
(set: $network_failed to true)
(set: $equipment to it - 1)

The computer network crashes. The control panel goes blank, and the crew has to run the base by hand until it's rebooted.
]
(else-if: $roll <= 60)[
(set: $comms_failed to true)
(set: $equipment to it - 1)

Communication and navigation go down. The base can't reach Earth, and the rover can't find its way back until it's fixed.
]
(else:)[
Nothing breaks this time. The systems still need service, and the risk is still there.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Investigation Tent {"position":"2575,1200","size":"100,100"}
INVESTIGATION LAB

A sealed tent with white tables and a computer that analyzes data. Labs like this let scientists use the unique conditions of space to run experiments that prepare us for deep-space trips. What they learn also helps improve life on Earth.

To open the lab you need two things: data to analyze and energy to run the equipment. The results get sent to Earth.

(if: $lab_done is true)[
The data is already on its way to Earth.

[[Back to the crater->Investigation Tent]]
]
(else-if: $data < 1)[
The lab stays closed. There's no data to analyze.

[[Back to the crater->Investigation Tent]]
]
(else-if: $energy < 1)[
The lab stays closed. There's no energy to run the equipment.

[[Back to the crater->Investigation Tent]]
]
(else:)[
[[Look at the analyzer->Lab Mission]]

[[Back to the crater->Investigation Tent]]
]


:: Lab Fast {"position":"2575,1450","size":"100,100"}
(set: $energy to it - 1)
(set: $roll to (random: 1, 100))

(if: $roll <= 10)[
(set: $data to 0)

Halfway through, the analyzer crashes and wipes the files. All the data is gone, and there's no way to get it back.
]
(else:)[
(set: $lab_done to true)
(set: $data_sent to true)

The quick analysis works. You send the results to Earth.
]

[[Back to map->Mars Map]]


:: Lab Mission {"position":"2575,1325","size":"100,100"}
You have $data of 5 pieces of data ready. They need to be analyzed and sent to Earth.

Energy left: $energy

[[Analyze it fast. It uses little energy, but there's a 10% chance something goes wrong and you lose all the data.->Lab Fast]]

(if: $energy >= 2)[(link-goto: "Analyze it carefully. It uses a lot of energy, but you get all the data.", "Lab Full")]
(else:)[Analyze it carefully. (Not enough energy for this option. You need at least 2.)]




:: Launch Day {"position":"3200,800","size":"100,100"}
LAUNCH DAY

The engines start, and the ship lifts off from Mars. The crew is on its way home.

This is your mission log.

WHAT YOU PROTECTED
(if: $data_sent is true)[- The radiation data reached Earth.
]
(if: $lab_done is true)[- The science results were analyzed.
]
(if: $food_lost is not true)[- The food survived the storm.
]
(if: $equipment_damaged is not true)[- The equipment came through the storm.
]

WHAT IT COST
(if: $food_lost is true)[- The food in the freezer spoiled in the storm.
]
(if: $equipment_damaged is true)[- The storm damaged the equipment.
]
(if: $data_lost is true)[- Some science data was lost.
]
(if: $thermo_failed is true)[- The heating and air system failed.
]
(if: $network_failed is true)[- The computer network crashed.
]
(if: $comms_failed is true)[- Communications went down.
]
(if: $mold_found is true)[- Mold ruined a tray of plants.
]
(if: $plants_stunted is true)[- The cold slowed the plants down.
]
(if: $robot_glitch is true)[- The robot's software froze mid-job.
]
(if: $comms_dip is true)[- The radio and lights went out when the arm started moving.
]

Every choice you made protected something and cost something else. There was no perfect answer.

What would you protect next time?

[[Play again->START]]


